+        # [CAIOS] Open WebUI must not reach vLLM through the front door.
+        #
+        # For "both", the two services are in the same allocation, but upstream
+        # hands Open WebUI the PUBLIC HTTPS endpoint of vLLM — so the chat
+        # interface leaves the node, crosses DNS and Traefik, and comes back to
+        # a port it could have reached directly. On any deployment whose TLS is
+        # signed by its own CA, aiohttp then raises CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED,
+        # which Open WebUI catches and reports as an EMPTY MODEL LIST behind an
+        # HTTP 200. A chat interface that logs in perfectly and has nothing to
+        # talk to, with the cause visible only in the container's stderr.
+        #
+        # Same reasoning as the two helper tasks in our nomad.hcl (D-36), and
+        # the same fix: address the allocation. ${NOMAD_ADDR_vllm} is left alone
+        # by safe_substitute and interpolated by the Nomad client at launch.
+        #
+        # Only "both" is touched. "open-webui" standalone must keep pointing at
+        # whatever endpoint the user supplied, which is the whole point of it.
+        if user_conf["llm"]["type"] == "both":
+            api_endpoint = "http://${NOMAD_ADDR_vllm}/v1"
